{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_aotm4kj557q4yrdc457u6fps5vyjxzrsw7z5smwodyzm7gcl7eba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four phases pass. Summary:\n\n## Phase A — both build\n| program | build | run |\n|---|---|---|\n| C | `cd c_src && mkdir -p build && cd build && cmake .. && cmake --build .` | `c_src/build/driver` |\n| Rust | `cd translation && cargo build --release` | `translation/target/release/driver` |\n\nBoth compile clean, no errors or warnings. No source changes were needed to compile.\n\n## Phase B/C — differential tests\n`translation/tests/differential.rs`: **24 tests**, each spawning both binaries as subprocesses and comparing stdout bytes, stderr bytes, and exit status *including the terminating signal*. Nothing is linked as a library.\n\nKey structural insight: reads share one `stdin`, so the **first** line feeds `goodB2G()` and the **second** feeds `bad()`; `fgets(buf,14,...)` stores only 13 bytes, so longer lines get *split* between the two sinks.\n\n## Three real mismatches found and fixed\n\n1. **Frame-smashing indices.** Second-line values `16,17,18,19,26,27` overlap `bad()`'s saved frame pointer / return address. C dies from SIGSEGV with *both streams empty* (block-buffered stdout is never flushed); the Rust printed 126 bytes and exited 0. Verified 100/100 reproducible per index, 0/100 for every other index in 10..300.\n\n2. **The far-OOB threshold was a wrong constant.** The Rust hard-coded 5010. There is *no* correct constant — the distance from `bad()`'s frame to the stack top depends on argv+environment size (a 60 KB env var shifts it ~16000 slots) plus a per-exec random offset. Replaced with the rule the hardware actually applies: read the `[stack]` mapping end from `/proc/self/maps` and fault when `&buffer[0] + 4*idx` reaches it. This now tracks C across tiny, normal, and 64 KB-padded environments.\n\n3. **`INT_MAX` index: SIGBUS vs SIGSEGV.** Not a translation bug — the C disagrees with *itself* (14× SIGBUS / 26× SIGSEGV over 40 runs).\n\n## Honest handling of irreducible non-determinism\nTwo input regions are not a function of the input in the C itself (stack-top band; extreme indices). Rather than deleting those cases, the harness gives **both** programs an identical 64 KB `DIFFTEST_STACK_PAD` env var, which pins the layout so indices ≤17000 are reliably invisible and ≥22000 reliably fault — turning previously untestable ground into exact-equality assertions. The two genuinely random regions are asserted on the property the C *does* hold to: outcomes are one of exactly two shapes, or death by signal with empty streams.\n\n## Phase D — gate\n- Both build clean ✅\n- `cargo test` passes — 24 passed, 0 failed, **0 ignored**, in 3 debug + 3 release runs, plus under a minimal ambient environment ✅\n- Independent verification outside cargo: 704 exhaustive index pairs + 600 fuzz cases (random byte soup, whitespace/sign torture) → **0 mismatches** ✅\n- `c_src/` unmodified — md5 of `main.c` and `CMakeLists.txt` unchanged; only the out-of-tree `build/` dir added (and the suite rebuilds it if absent) ✅\n- `translation/ERRORS.md` records each mismatch, its cause, and the measurement tables ✅"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2557,"cache_read_input_tokens":97568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2557,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5b3f3ed-1cac-489d-b784-afa61a974c15","uuid":"4e4315c9-0238-46fc-85c0-087b0d75ac14","timestamp":"2026-08-28T11:21:29.056Z"}
